dune is one of the most famous sci-fi  books ever the story of paul atreides  rise to power is widely read and been  made into movies and tv shows but this  book is not the whole story of dune  frank herbert wrote six dune books and  it's only in these sequels that the true  meaning of june is revealed the dune  sequel books get weird paul's son  transforms into a worm god and rules for  thousands of years duncan idaho gets  resurrected hundreds of times there's an  invasion by dominatrixes from space and  genetically modified cat people and  chairs made out of living dogs and each  book is full of secret plots and  abstract philosophical ideas it would  take many videos to fully explore these  books so first what's the basic story  what happens in frank herbert's six june  books  in book one house atreides takes over  the desert planet arrakis land of sand  worms and spice but they're attacked by  the hakonens and the emperor paul  atreides unlocks a powerful mind that  can see into the future he becomes a  religious leader to the native fremen  and falls in love with cheney he defeats  the hakonens and defeats emperor shirdam  and paul becomes emperor of the universe  so book one seems to be a classic story  of a hero fulfilling his destiny and  defeating evil  but in book two june messiah paul being  emperor is a disaster the fremen kill  billions of people in their holy war and  paul can't stop the violence his  religion is out of his control  a conspiracy of powerful people plot to  destroy paul led by gaius mahayam and by  paul's wife princess ireland with a  spacing guild navigator and a tlalaksu  face dancer and paul's own fremen high  priest these guys have an elaborate plan  to destroy paul using a cryptic dwarf  called bajaz who manipulates a  resurrected version of duncan idaho who  is now a mentat philosopher with robot  eyes  paul knows there's a plot against him  but he allows some of their plan to  happen anyway because he's afraid of  even worse possible futures happening  instead seeing the future is a curse a  trap that takes away paul's free will  paul gets blinded by a nuclear weapon so  he relies on his visions to see like neo  in the matrix iii  cheney dies giving birth to twins lato  the second and genema  paul wants to escape his grief and  politics and destiny so he walks into  the desert to die  so in june messiah polls rise as a  heroic leader turns out to have been a  terrible mistake he loses everything he  loves and gets billions of people killed  the message is that religious and  political leaders are dangerous blindly  following a messiah or a vision or plan  can lead to disaster  book three is children of dune paul's  sister alia rules the universe on behalf  of young lato and genema but alia's mind  gets possessed taken over by the memory  of the baron vladimir haarkonen  turns out that the baron was alia and  paul's grandfather and his personality  corrupts alia's mind and leads her  government into decline  it turns out that changing the  environment of a racket to have water  and plants is a disaster because without  desert there's no sand worms and no  spice and fremen desert culture starts  to die  paul turns out to be still alive as a  mysterious desert preacher he criticizes  the atreides religion and government but  ends up getting stabbed to death by his  own priests  when cecio carino the daughter of the  old emperor shaddam plots against the  atreides she tries to kill leto and  genema with laser tigers so lato fakes  his own death and gets super high in the  desert to unlock his mind and lato sees  a possible future that could save  humanity from extinction a plan called  the golden path  lato transforms his own body so he'll  become part sandworm and will rule the  universe for thousands of years  jessica deals with the carinos by  converting their heir to the bene jesuit  alia kills herself to kill the baron  within her and wormboy lato becomes  emperor plato's plan will apparently  save the human species but to be the  savior he has to give up his humanity  and become a monstrous tyrant dune  rejects the heroic messiah paul and  instead turns to a darker more  complicated leader  book four is god emperor of dune set  thousands of years after the previous  books lato rules the universe with an  iron fist his plan the golden path is to  oppress humanity for thousands of years  to teach the species to want freedom to  grow stronger and to think for ourselves  leto also breeds the atreides bloodline  to create siona atreides siona has a  special gene that makes her invisible to  people who can see the future so siona's  genes will free humanity from the  control of prescient people  lato falls in love with a woman called  hui  trapped in his monstrous worm body lato  is tormented by the loss of his humanity  his tragic self-sacrifice to save the  species  over the centuries lato resurrects  duncan idaho over and over and he allows  duncan and siona to rebel against him he  teaches duncan and siona so they grow  strong enough to eventually destroy him  in the end duncan and siona kill later  by using the blind obedience of nayla a  fanatic of lato's religion lato's dying  body rejuvenates the sandworms and spice  on arrakis and humanity is finally freed  from his control after millennia of  oppression humanity bursts out across  the universe in the scattering a mass  migration into space  humanity expands and evolves to save it  from stagnation and extinction just as  lato planned his golden path gives  humanity a universe of infinite  possibilities  book five heretics of dune is set  another thousand years in the future the  bene jesuit control much of the old  empire but a new threat comes from the  scattering the honoured matres are a  wild offshoot from the bene jesuit who  use sex to enslave people the beni  jesuit train a girl called shiana who  can control sandworms and they hope to  breed her with a new resurrected duncan  idaho and to use her as a religious  force to control people  but there's also a plot by the  talaylaksu a bunch of religious genetic  scientists who look like creepy grey  elves the tlailaxu secretly modified  this new duncan giving him special sex  powers that terrify the honored matres  bene jesuit leader teraza uses duncan to  lure the honored matres into destroying  the planet arrakis because by killing  the planet's sand worms they destroy the  remnants of emperor lato's consciousness  and end his influence on the universe  the benejezer at take a sand worm to  make spice on their own planet called  chapter house terraza is helped by miles  teg a legendary atreides mentat soldier  who sacrifices himself and dies on  arrakis  in book six chapter house dune the  honoured matres rampage across the  empire hunting to exterminate the bene  jesuit the beni jesuit go into hiding on  the planet chapter house under the  leadership of dawi o'drady an unusually  rebellious reverend mother who wants her  sisterhood to change and evolve to  survive this crisis  o'drady creates a young clone of miles  tegh who is her father and she trains a  captured honored matre mabella to be a  bene jesuit  mabella and duncan fall in love  teg leads an attack on the honoured  matres but the matres defeat tag with a  secret weapon and they kill a drady so  mebella infiltrates and takes over the  honored matres from within then she  merges the honored matres with the benny  jesuit assimilating them to create a new  stronger sisterhood mobella has changed  so duncan decides to leave her he and  shyanna steal a spaceship and escape the  sisterhood along with the last living  claelaksu master and a secret group of  jewish people and some sandworms and a  van gogh painting together they start a  new journey free in the infinite  universe  in the final chapter we see a mysterious  elderly couple called daniel and marty  these two are apparently advanced face  dancers from the scattering who escaped  the control of the tla laksu but daniel  and marty also seem to represent the  author frank herbert and his wife  beverly  as they work in their garden they break  the fourth wall a little chatting about  june's characters and the unfinished  plotlines like the tlaxu they admit that  the characters got away from them they  are now beyond the author's control  the book ends with a loving tribute to  bev who died the previous year and the  year after publication frank died  so frank never wrote a neat final  conclusion to the june series but this  open-ended last chapter fits the central  themes of june the characters get  freedom and self-determination not even  the author controls them anymore and  daniel and marty in their garden show  the simple human warmth that is the  emotional heart of dune  dune was never really about the plot as  much as it's about the ideas a  philosophy of the mind of thinking of  politics technology of how to live in a  chaotic universe so we're making a video  called the philosophy of june to explore  the themes and big ideas of the series  we're also going to cover the new game  of thrones tv show house of the dragon  which is based on a book called fire and  blood  fire and blood and the entire dune  series are available on audiobook you  can get any one of these for free right  now at audible.com asx sign up for a  premium plus trial membership and you  can choose an audiobook to keep even if  you cancel the trial you could get the  dune audio collection with readings and  commentary by frank herbert himself  membership also includes unlimited  access to thousands of audiobooks and  shows in the audible plus catalog sign  up at audible.com asx or text asx to 500  500  thanks for watching and thanks to the  patrons including j lee 60 micah prude  reuven dewenda hill1030 dylan elliott  and rilhonn cheers  you
 

